    "interpretation": "The compiled isolated-mode source disables cross-GPU tracker dependencies and returns from semaphore-pool initialization before mapping another provider's existing semaphore pages. New semaphore backing is CPU-mapped and remains local to its owner GPU. If GPU initialization fails before publication, add_gpu routes through remove_gpu/deinit_gpu; null channel-manager and semaphore-pool cleanup is guarded, while any partially installed foreign pool mappings are removed before the RM address space is destroyed. After the semaphore step, the ordinary channel path queries copy-engine caps by device owner, allocates TSGs by address-space owner, allocates channels by TSG owner, and programs the page directory by address-space owner. The paging-channel callback remains unsupported, but R580 calls it only for SR-IOV Heavy proxy pools. These are static route and source-order findings only. They do not prove runtime GPU initialization, RM acceptance, or cross-GPU UVM/P2P behavior.",
